You approach the Mayor's manor and knock firmly on the heavy wooden door. After a long moment, you hear footsteps approaching from inside. The door opens just a crack, and you see a haggard man with dark circles under his eyes—Mayor Aldric Hollow.

"Thank the gods!" he gasps, tears forming in his eyes. "An adventurer! Please, come in quickly!" He pulls you inside and immediately bolts the door behind you, checking multiple locks with trembling hands.

The Mayor looks terrible—unwashed, unshaven, his fine clothes wrinkled and stained. He's clearly been living in fear for days, perhaps weeks.

"Three days ago," he begins without preamble, his voice cracking with emotion, "my daughter Lydia was taken. Robed figures—cultists—dragged her down into the catacombs beneath the cemetery. I'm too terrified to go after her myself. The undead attack this house every night."

He provides you with supplies:

3 HEALING POTIONS (each restores 4 STAMINA)

SILVER DAGGER (+2 damage vs undead)

50 Gold Pieces

A MAP OF HOLLOW'S END (his own, marked with the dangers he knows)

MAYOR'S LEDGER (if you don't have it)

Add these items to your Adventure Sheet.

The Mayor's offer is clear: rescue Lydia from the catacombs, and he'll give you the Silver Key—one of the three critical items needed to bind the Widow permanently.

