You take a moment to review everything you've learned about the curse:

THE CURSE OF HOLLOW'S END - Complete History:

242 years ago, Eliza Hollow married Thomas Ashford against her father's wishes. Mordecai Hollow wanted Eliza to marry a noble for political gain. During the wedding ceremony, Mordecai's men murdered Thomas before the altar. They then used forbidden necromancy to bind Eliza's spirit with silver chains, preventing her from seeking justice even in death.

The binding was designed to last only one generation—long enough for the guilty to die in peace. But it was never meant to be permanent. Each generation, the binding weakened. Now, 242 years later, it has failed completely.

To bind the Widow permanently, you need:

1. SILVER KEY (for physical binding)

2. HER TRUE NAME: ELIZA HOLLOW (for spiritual authority)

3. MIDNIGHT TIMING (for maximum power)

